  "Correct child answers do not automatically make the parent's answer correct. Sorted halves still need a valid merge, and partial paths may need compatible endpoints. State the original output condition and show the combine step establishes it from the child contracts. This is often the central inductive argument in a divide-and-conquer proof.",
