  "The cost of transforming an input is part of the algorithm using the reduction. A fast solver cannot rescue a preprocessing step that enumerates exponentially many objects. Bound both transformation size and construction time, then include solution decoding as well. For polynomial-time efficiency, each stage must fit a polynomial bound in the original input length.",
