  "Two histories have the same future answer only if the state includes everything the rules depend on. That includes the next player and, in games with repetition rules, relevant history as well as the board. Once the full state agrees, the legal continuations and outcomes agree. An incomplete board-only description can incorrectly merge positions with different permitted futures.",
