  "With a fixed original string, the index i uniquely identifies the suffix starting at i. If the dictionary is also fixed and there are no history-dependent constraints, that index completely determines the remaining question. A memo table can therefore store one boolean per suffix. Additional restrictions, such as a word-count budget, would require extra state in the cache key.",
