  "Every key in the interval is a possible root. For each one, add optimal left and right subtree costs plus the interval's total frequency, then choose the least result. Trying all roots makes the recurrence complete. Direct recursive evaluation repeats many interval problems, so the mathematical recurrence can be correct even when its naive execution is expensive.",
