  "A prefix-free code never lets one complete codeword begin another. For example, {0, 10, 11} is prefix-free, while {0, 01} is not because reading 0 could be a complete symbol or the start of 01. Prefix freedom lets a decoder know exactly when a symbol ends as it reads the bitstream.",
