  "The selected edges begin as isolated vertices and remain acyclic as safe edges join different components. Thus the intermediate structure is a forest, potentially containing several trees. Acyclicity alone does not guarantee minimum weight; the stronger invariant is that the selected forest can be extended to an MST. The edge-selection rule must preserve both properties.",
