  "Strong connectivity requires a directed path from u to v and another from v to u. A one-way road from u to v is insufficient. The two paths need not use the same edges in reverse, because those reverse edges may not exist. Mutual reachability groups vertices that can circulate between one another despite the graph's directions.",
