  "Replace each SCC by one vertex and retain edges between different components. If the resulting graph had a directed cycle, the components on that cycle could reach one another in both directions and should have been one SCC. This contradiction makes the condensation graph acyclic. Remove internal self-edges during contraction so they do not obscure that structure.",
