  "A forward search from v finds everything v can reach. A search from v after reversing all edges finds everything that can reach v in the original graph. Their intersection contains exactly the vertices satisfying both directions, which is v's SCC. Taking the union would include one-way relationships and therefore produce an incorrect component.",
  "Reversing an edge changes u to v into v to u. Consequently, a path from x to v in the original becomes a path from v to x in the reversed graph. One ordinary search from v on that reversal finds all original predecessors reachable by any path. This avoids launching a separate search from every possible predecessor.",
