  "Every vertex reaches itself by a zero-edge path, giving reflexivity. Mutual reachability is symmetric by definition. If u and v are mutually reachable and v and w are mutually reachable, concatenating paths gives both directions between u and w, establishing transitivity. These properties make strong connectivity an equivalence relation whose classes are the SCCs.",
