  "Independent forward-and-reverse searches can repeatedly scan the same graph while rediscovering component relationships. Linear SCC methods avoid that repetition by using DFS finishing order or equivalent structural information to choose safe component starts. The improvement comes from coordinated traversal, not from changing the definition of mutual reachability. Each vertex and edge participates only a bounded number of times overall.",
