  "The first vertex discovered in an SCC can reach every other member before its DFS call finishes. Those members become descendants, while its own parent cannot be in the component because no member was discovered earlier. This establishes the component's distinguished DFS root. The chosen root can change when traversal order changes, even though the SCC's vertex set does not.",
