  "For an edge u to v in a DAG, v finishes before u: it is either explored beneath u or was already finished when the edge was examined. An active target would imply a cycle and is excluded. Reversing finish order therefore places u before v for every edge, which is exactly the topological requirement.",
  "DFSAll loops over all vertices and launches DFS at each still-unseen one. This reaches regions unavailable from the first root while preserving earlier marks. It is needed for whole-graph properties such as cycle detection and complete timestamping. In directed graphs, the resulting forest roots do not directly correspond to SCCs, so additional reasoning is required for component labels.",
