  "The generic method leaves the choice of tense edge unspecified. Different schedules lead to BFS-like, topological, Dijkstra-style, or Bellman-Ford methods under their respective assumptions. The schedule controls efficiency and may require additional invariants. A priority queue is not a universal replacement for all schedules, especially when negative weights invalidate the usual settled-distance argument.",
