  "For each of V sources, an edge-relaxation pass examines E edges, and up to V minus one passes suffice without negative cycles. This gives O(V squared E) relaxation work, plus table initialization and any copying overhead. On dense graphs the bound becomes quartic. Be explicit about sparse degenerate cases and implementation overhead rather than treating E as automatically at least V.",
