  "When the total allowance is 2L edges, choose a split so both pieces use at most L. A shorter route may split at an endpoint, leaving one zero-edge piece. This is why zero diagonal costs are useful. The guarantee concerns the allowed edge count; it does not mean the two halves have equal weight.",
